# qwen3.5-4b-jetson — NVIDIA Jetson Orin (8 GB) tutor model, Qwen3.5 4B tier
#
# Build:   ollama create qwen3.5-4b-jetson -f infra/ollama/Modelfile.qwen3.5-4b-jetson
# Use:     ./chat.py --qwen3.5-4b
#          or pick it in /admin/ (ModelConfig, purpose=tutoring)
#
# Same reasoning as Modelfile.qwen3.5-2b-jetson — read that one for the full
# story. In short: apps/llm/model_profiles.py can only pin num_ctx on requests
# this codebase builds. The grader's Tier-2 verifier reaches Ollama through
# instructor's OPENAI-COMPATIBLE endpoint (POST /v1/chat/completions), which has
# no num_ctx field, so on a bare tag it lands at Ollama's 4096 default. Ollama
# keys a runner on (model, params), so that is a second runner — and under
# OLLAMA_MAX_LOADED_MODELS=1 the two evict each other on every graded turn.
#
# A Modelfile PARAMETER applies on every endpoint, which is the only way to
# cover callers we do not construct requests for.
FROM qwen3.5:4b

# Must match local_ollama/qwen3.5-4b-jetson in apps/llm/model_profiles.py.
# 16384 holds the tutor's system prompt + tool schemas + a turn of output; at
# the stock window the KV cache plus weights exceeds this box's free memory.
PARAMETER num_ctx 16384

# Qwen3.5's own recommended sampling (framework §3.3), restated so the tag is
# self-describing and the OpenAI-compatible path inherits them too.
PARAMETER temperature 0.7
PARAMETER top_p 0.8
PARAMETER top_k 20
